## TL;DR  

* **`map.setFog()` → `map.setSky()`** (and add a `sky` object to your style).  
* **Free-camera APIs (`getFreeCameraOptions`, `setFreeCameraOptions`, `FreeCameraOptions`) do not exist in MapLibre.**  
  Use the **camera-calculation helpers** (`calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation`, `calculateCameraOptionsFromTo`) and then call `jumpTo`, `easeTo` or `flyTo`.  
* The rest of the migration (package, namespace, token, style URL, plugins, etc.) is the same as described in the **Mapbox → MapLibre** skill you already have.  

Below is a focused “fix-the-broken-features” guide plus a quick sanity-check checklist to make sure the rest of the migration is solid.

---

## 1. Why Those Calls are Broken

| Feature | Mapbox GL JS v2 | MapLibre GL JS |
|---------|----------------|----------------|
| `map.setFog()` / `fog` style property | **Implemented** (adds a simple atmospheric fog layer) | **Not implemented** – the API was never added to MapLibre. |
| `map.getFreeCameraOptions()` / `map.setFreeCameraOptions()` / `FreeCameraOptions` | **Implemented** (allows you to set a camera by lng/lat/alt/rotation) | **Not implemented** – MapLibre only knows the classic `center`, `zoom`, `pitch`, `bearing` (plus `elevation`/`roll` from v5). |

MapLibre deliberately **does not ship any Mapbox-v2-only APIs**. The library stopped at the v1.13 codebase, and the Mapbox team added those methods *after* the fork. So you didn’t “do something wrong”; you’re simply trying to call APIs that don’t exist in MapLibre.

The fix is to **use the MapLibre equivalents** (or emulate the effect yourself).

---

## 2. Re-creating Fog → Sky

### 2.1 Add a `sky` object to your style

MapLibre’s atmospheric effect lives in the **`sky`** object (spec-level, not a layer). You can add it directly in the style JSON or via `map.setSky()` at runtime.

**Style-JSON example (add to the root of the style):**

```json
{
  "version": 8,
  "sources": { … },
  "layers": [ … ],
  "sky": {
    "type": "sky",
    "sky-type": "atmosphere",          // "gradient" is also allowed
    "sky-color": "#199EF3",
    "horizon-color": "#ffffff",
    "fog-color": "#0000ff",
    "fog-ground-blend": 0.5,
    "horizon-fog-blend": 0.5,
    "sky-horizon-blend": 0.5,
    "atmosphere-blend": 1.0
  }
}
```

If you prefer to set it programmatically (e.g. toggle fog on/off), you can call:

```js
// map is a maplibregl.Map instance
map.setSky({
  "sky-type": "atmosphere",
  "sky-color": "#199EF3",
  "horizon-color": "#ffffff",
  "fog-color": "#0000ff",
  "fog-ground-blend": 0.5,
  "horizon-fog-blend": 0.5,
  "sky-horizon-blend": 0.5,
  "atmosphere-blend": 1.0
});
```

**Key points**

* `sky` replaces the old `fog` object.  
* The property names are **different** (`sky-color` vs. `color`, `fog-ground-blend` vs. `ground-blend`, etc.).  
* The `sky` object is **part of the style**, not a layer you add with `addLayer`.  
* If you want a *simple* fog-only effect, you can keep `sky-type: "gradient"` and only set the fog-related fields.

### 2.2 Updating existing code

```js
// BEFORE (Mapbox)
map.setFog({
  "color": "#ffffff",
  "high-color": "#ffffff",
  "space-color": "#000000",
  "horizon-blend": 0.3
});

// AFTER (MapLibre)
map.setSky({
  "sky-type": "atmosphere",
  "sky-color": "#ffffff",
  "horizon-color": "#ffffff",
  "fog-color": "#000000",
  "horizon-fog-blend": 0.3
});
```

If you have a UI toggle that calls `map.setFog(null)` to turn fog off, replace it with:

```js
map.setSky(null); // removes the sky object (no atmosphere)
```

---

## 3. Re-creating Free-Camera Controls

### 3.1 What you probably had in Mapbox

```js
// Example: look at a point from a specific altitude/tilt
const cam = map.getFreeCameraOptions();
cam.center = [lng, lat];
cam.altitude = 2000;          // metres above ground
cam.pitch = 45;
cam.bearing = 30;
map.setFreeCameraOptions(cam);
```

### 3.2 MapLibre’s approach

MapLibre works with **`CameraOptions`** (center, zoom, pitch, bearing, elevation, roll). There is **no `FreeCameraOptions` class**. To compute a camera that mimics “look from altitude X at point Y”, you can:

1. **Calculate the camera options** using the helper that converts a *camera position* (lng/lat/alt) + orientation into the classic `center/zoom/pitch/bearing` set.
2. **Apply the options** with `jumpTo`, `easeTo`, or `flyTo`.

#### Helper: `calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation`

```js
/**
 * @param {maplibregl.LngLat} lngLat   – target point you want to look at
 * @param {number} altitude            – metres above the ellipsoid (or ground, depending on terrain)
 * @param {number} bearing             – clockwise from north, degrees
 * @param {number} pitch               – degrees, 0 = looking straight down
 * @param {number} roll                – degrees, clockwise rotation around the view axis (optional)
 * @returns {maplibregl.CameraOptions}
 */
const camOpts = map.calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation(
  [lng, lat],          // lngLat you want to *center* on
  altitude,            // altitude in metres
  bearing,             // bearing
  pitch,               // pitch
  0                    // roll (optional, default 0)
);
```

Now feed the result to any camera transition method:

```js
// Instant jump (no animation)
map.jumpTo(camOpts);

// Smooth animation
map.easeTo(camOpts);   // or map.flyTo(camOpts) for a “fly” effect
```

#### Helper: `calculateCameraOptionsFromTo` (look-at from one point to another)

If you need a *look-at* where the camera is positioned at `from` and points at `to`:

```js
const camOpts = map.calculateCameraOptionsFromTo(
  [fromLng, fromLat],   // camera position
  fromAltitude,         // altitude of the camera
  [toLng, toLat],       // point you want to look at
  toAltitude            // altitude of the target (usually 0)
);
map.easeTo(camOpts);
```

### 3.3 Quick migration snippet

```js
// MAPBOX (broken after migration)
const cam = map.getFreeCameraOptions();
cam.center = [12.4924, 41.8902];
cam.altitude = 1500;
cam.pitch = 45;
cam.bearing = 20;
map.setFreeCameraOptions(cam);

// MAPLIBRE (working)
const camOpts = map.calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation(
  [12.4924, 41.8902], // lng/lat you want centered
  1500,               // altitude in metres
  20,                 // bearing
  45,                 // pitch
  0                   // roll (optional)
);
map.easeTo(camOpts);   // or map.jumpTo(camOpts) for no animation
```

### 3.4 What about `elevation` and `roll`?

* **`elevation`** (MapLibre v5+) lets you offset the camera vertically *relative* to the ground (useful with terrain). It is part of `CameraOptions` and can be set directly:

```js
map.easeTo({ center: [lng, lat], zoom: 14, pitch: 45, bearing: 30, elevation: 200 });
```

* **`roll`** is also a `CameraOptions` field (v5+). Use it if you need a “banked” view.

