## 4. Full “Fog-and-Free-Camera” Migration Checklist

| ✅ Item | What to do | Example |
|--------|------------|---------|
| **Add sky to style** | Either edit your style JSON (`sky` object) **or** call `map.setSky()` at runtime. | `map.setSky({ "sky-type": "atmosphere", "sky-color": "#199EF3", … })` |
| **Remove `map.setFog` calls** | Delete or replace with `setSky`. | `map.setFog(null)` → `map.setSky(null)` |
| **Replace free-camera code** | Use `calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation` (or `calculateCameraOptionsFromTo`) + `jumpTo/easeTo/flyTo`. | See code snippet above. |
| **Update any UI that exposed fog/camera sliders** | Ensure the UI now updates the `sky` object or calls the new camera helper. | Slider → `map.setSky({ "fog-ground-blend": value })` |
| **Verify MapLibre version** | v6+ is ES-module-only; make sure you import `* as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl'` (or `{Map}`) and that your bundler supports ESM. | `import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';` |
| **Check CSS class prefixes** | `mapboxgl-` → `maplibregl-` (e.g., `.maplibregl-ctrl`). | Update any custom CSS. |
| **Remove `mapboxgl.accessToken`** | No token needed for MapLibre itself. | Delete `mapboxgl.accessToken = '…'`. |
| **Swap style URL** | Use a non-Mapbox style (OpenFreeMap, your own, or a style you exported & rewired). | `style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty'`. |
| **Test** | Load the map, open dev-tools, ensure no `Uncaught ReferenceError: map.setFog is not a function` or similar. | - |
| **Optional: Validate style** | `npx gl-style-validate style.json` (install `@maplibre/maplibre-gl-style-spec`). | - |

If you run through the checklist and still see errors, the most common culprits are:

* **Forgot to rename a single `mapboxgl` reference** (e.g., a stray `new mapboxgl.Popup()`).
* **Using a Mapbox-only style URL** (`mapbox://styles/...`) – the map will fail to load tiles.
* **Using a Mapbox-only plugin** that still expects `mapboxgl` on the global window (e.g., some older geocoder widgets). Swap to the MapLibre-compatible fork or a pure-JS alternative.

