## 4. Double-Check Other v2-Only Features

| Feature | Mapbox v2 | MapLibre status | What to do |
|---------|-----------|----------------|------------|
| **Globe projection** (`map.setProjection('globe')`) | ✅ (v2) | ✅ (v5+) | Works unchanged – just call `map.setProjection('globe')`. |
| **Terrain exaggeration** (`map.setTerrain({source:..., exaggeration: 2})`) | ✅ | ✅ (same API) | Ensure the DEM source is not a `mapbox://` URL. |
| **Custom glyphs / sprite URLs** | `glyphs: "mapbox://fonts/...` | Must be absolute URLs (e.g. `https://mytileserver.com/fonts/{fontstack}/{range}.pbf`) | Update the style JSON. |
| **Mapbox-specific expressions** (`["image", "mapbox://..."]`) | ✅ | ❌ (needs a URL that resolves to an image) | Replace with a URL to a hosted PNG/SVG or a data URI. |
| **Mapbox-only plugins** (e.g., `mapbox-gl-geocoder`) | ✅ | Some have MapLibre forks (`@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder`) or you can use open alternatives (e.g., `leaflet-geocoder`, `pelias`). | Swap the import and adjust any `mapboxgl` references. |

If you encounter any other “unknown method” errors, search the **MapLibre API reference** (`https://maplibre.org/maplibre-gl-js/docs/API/`) rather than the Mapbox docs.

---

## 5. Full Minimal Example (ES-module, MapLibre v6)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre – fog → sky & free-camera demo</title>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    #map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }
    .control { position:absolute; top:10px; left:10px; background:#fff; padding:5px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>
<div class="control">
  <button id="raise">Raise 500 m</button>
  <button id="sky">Toggle sky</button>
</div>

<script type="module">
  import * as maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs';

  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty', // any non-Mapbox style
    center: [-122.42, 37.78],
    zoom: 12,
    pitch: 45,
    bearing: 0,
    antialias: true // needed for sky rendering
  });

  // ---- SKY (replaces fog) ----
  let skyEnabled = false;
  function enableSky() {
    map.setSky({
      "sky-type": "atmosphere",
      "sky-color": "#88ccee",
      "horizon-color": "#ffffff",
      "fog-color": "#cceeff",
      "sky-horizon-blend": 0.5,
      "atmosphere-blend": 0.8
    });
    skyEnabled = true;
  }
  function disableSky() {
    map.setSky(null); // removes the sky layer
    skyEnabled = false;
  }

  document.getElementById('sky').addEventListener('click', () => {
    skyEnabled ? disableSky() : enableSky();
  });

  // ---- FREE-CAMERA (altitude) ----
  let altitude = 0; // meters above ground
  const ALT_STEP = 500;

  document.getElementById('raise').addEventListener('click', () => {
    altitude += ALT_STEP;
    const cam = map.calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation(
      map.getCenter(),
      altitude,
      map.getBearing(),
      map.getPitch(),
      0
    );
    map.easeTo(cam);
  });

  // Optional: add navigation controls
  map.addControl(new maplibregl.NavigationControl());

  // Wait for the style to load before we can call setSky / camera helpers
  map.on('style.load', () => {
    // start with sky off; you can enable it here if you want
    // enableSky();
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

*The example demonstrates the two most common “v2-only” features you mentioned and shows the exact MapLibre replacements.*

---

## 6. Checklist – After Fixing the Two Features

| ✅ | Item |
|----|------|
| 1 | **Package** – `npm install maplibre-gl@^6` (or CDN ES-module). |
| 2 | **Imports / CSS** – `import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl'` + `import 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css'`. |
| 3 | **Namespace** – All `mapboxgl` → `maplibregl`. |
| 4 | **Access token** – Removed. |
| 5 | **Style URL** – Non-Mapbox (`https://tiles.openfreemap.org/...`, your own style JSON, or a hosted style from MapTiler, Martin, etc.). |
| 6 | **Fog → Sky** – Replace `map.setFog` with `map.setSky` and update any `fog` objects in style JSON. |
| 7 | **Free-camera** – Use `calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation` (or `calculateCameraOptionsFromTo`) + `jump
